@page "/docs/components/popover"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Popover
<PageTitle>Popover - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Popover</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="popover" />
        </div>
        <p>A floating panel anchored to a trigger, positioned with <a class="font-medium text-foreground" href="https://floating-ui.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Floating UI</a>. Click the trigger to toggle it; Escape or a click outside dismisses it. It is <strong>non-modal</strong> - the rest of the page stays interactive while it is open, and an outside click both closes the popover and acts on what you clicked.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(PopoverDefaultExample)"
                Description="Add the using once, then compose a trigger and a content panel. Any element can be the trigger via RenderAs." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="The full anatomy. Wrap the title and description in a header; drop in an optional BzPopoverArrow and use BzPopoverClose to dismiss from inside." />

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Portaling</h2>
        <p>While open, the panel moves itself to the document body, so no ancestor stacking context or overflow clip (a fixed sidebar, a transformed card, a scroll container) can cover or cut it. Positioning, focus and dismissal are unaffected. Set <code>Inline="true"</code> to render it in place instead: useful under CSS containment, for print, or in tests that assert on nearby markup. Note that a portaled surface is not reachable by ancestor CSS selectors; style it through its own Class or slot attributes.</p>
    </section>

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="Click to open. Focus moves into the panel; click outside or press Escape to close, and focus returns to the trigger."
          Example="typeof(PopoverDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom trigger element (RenderAs)"
          Description="When you need the trigger to be something other than a button - a link, a card, your own component - use RenderAs and splat the behaviour onto your element."
          Example="typeof(PopoverRenderAsTriggerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Arrow" Description="Drop an optional PopoverArrow inside the content to point back at the trigger. It is filled with the panel surface and shares the card's hairline ring and shadow, so it reads as the panel's tail rather than a flat sticker - and it rotates to whichever side the panel resolves to."
          Example="typeof(PopoverArrowExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With a form" Description="The panel is interactive - put inputs, buttons, anything inside. Widen it with a Class on PopoverContent."
          Example="typeof(PopoverFormExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Align" Description="Align sets where the panel sits along the trigger's edge - start, center, or end."
          Example="typeof(PopoverAlignExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sides" Description="Side sets the preferred edge the panel opens from - left, top, bottom, or right - flipping to the opposite side to stay in view. Drop in an optional PopoverArrow to point back at the trigger."
          Example="typeof(PopoverSidesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Controlled" Description="Drive the open state from the page with a two-way Open binding; PopoverClose closes it from inside the panel."
          Example="typeof(PopoverControlledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Restyle any part via Class - a brand-colored trigger and a content panel with a tinted surface, accented border, and a wider radius. Root-level utilities win over the skin, so these take effect."
          Example="typeof(PopoverCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Wrapped in a DirectionProvider with Arabic or Hebrew copy - the panel anchors and aligns mirrored to the right."
          Example="typeof(PopoverRtlExample)" />

</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzPopover",
        new CompositionNode("BzPopoverTrigger"),
        new CompositionNode("BzPopoverContent",
            new CompositionNode("BzPopoverHeader",
                new CompositionNode("BzPopoverTitle"),
                new CompositionNode("BzPopoverDescription")),
            new CompositionNode("BzPopoverArrow"),
            new CompositionNode("BzPopoverClose")));
}
